    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1079">

                <pb facs="0895" n="885" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg885"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Bacon, Leonard Lee: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kohler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-09T18:00:00+03:00">June 9, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 9—12:32 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1491. [To Nanking:] If Embassy to be requested renew efforts re Bacon visas
                    (reurtel 1182 to Department,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d1079-f1"/> repeated 35 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">34?</hi>] Moscow), desirable have any information
                    available re probable sailing date and point of departure.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 66, repeated Department 1491.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kohler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
